From 19514d076e5b8af8484cb4a438a6b7fff6908689 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 21:54:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add master tune (A4 reference pitch 415.3-466.2 Hz)

Settings > Tuning > Master tune (Hz) sets the reference pitch of A4 in
0.1 Hz steps (default 440.0).

- Synth tracks follow it: every oscillator type (waveforms, wavetables,
  samples, inputs, DX7) and the FM modulators, applied once at the end of
  Voice::calculatePhaseIncrements with an exact 64-bit multiply.
- Kit rows keep their exact pitch, audio clips are not touched.
- Changing it retunes notes that are already sounding (synth voices,
  CV outputs, external MIDI).
- CV outputs add the offset in cents.
- External MIDI instruments get RPN 1 (Channel Fine Tuning) on every
  channel they play, before the first note after a change or after
  playback starts. Nothing is sent while the firmware was never retuned.
- Stored as "masterTune" in CommunityFeatures.XML on the SD card (firmware
  that doesn't know it keeps it as an unknown setting). A value left in
  flash bytes 198-199 by earlier master-tune builds is migrated and those
  bytes are zero again once the settings file holds the value.
- At 440.0 Hz all paths are identical to the unmodified firmware.
- Project version set to 1.2.1 to match the release this is based on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
